"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.3.stable, 4.4.stable, 4.5.dev3.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a `MeshInstance3D` has a non-uniform scale which meets the following conditions, its lighting will flicker when it is rotated:\n- Two of the components have the ratio of **exactly** `0.9` between them (e.g. `1.0` and `0.9`)\n- The remaining component must have the same value as one of the other two.\nExamples of scales which will exhibit this issue:\n- `(1, 0.9, 1)`\n- `(0.9, 1, 0.9)`\n- `(2, 2, 1.8)`\n- `(3.6, 4, 4)`\nExamples of scales which will not exhibit this issue:\n- `(1, 0.9, 0.7)`\n- `(0.9, 0.9, 0.9)`\n\nThis happens in editor as well as runtime. It happens in all three renderers.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82573a1a-6701-49e9-aa69-05f43abcc4f2)\n\nEDIT:\n- Someone noted that the background is flickering as well - that is just a red herring from the GIF compression.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the attached project/scene, rotate the `MeshInstance3D` slowly, and note the flickering.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-report-2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20088559/bug-report-2.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/u